   This list is not an anarchy and there is no free market of PPL's. In
fact, the list "PPL" in the context of the list itself is a monopoly. There
is only one. If you disagree with it you can not contract with another except
to leave the list. So the "anarchist society" is not the list itself, but
the internet, and the Extropians list is a private community run by
a corporation.

  The "voluntary totalitarian subcommunity" does not attempt to impose its
will on people who are not members of the community. You are free to
join xtropy-l if you wish and no one will stop you. But on this list,
everyone is a contractor with the list management and you can't escape
that fact. If the list were a coffeehouse and you didn't like the management,
